      "text": "The geometric mean of two positive real numbers $a$ and $b$ is $\\sqrt{ab}$. Given that the geometric mean is $\\sqrt{3}$, we have:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{ab} = \\sqrt{3} \\implies ab = 3\n\\]\n\nThe harmonic mean of two positive real numbers $a$ and $b$ is $\\frac{2ab}{a+b}$. Given that the harmonic mean is $\\frac{3}{2}$, we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{2ab}{a+b} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting $ab = 3$ into the harmonic mean equation, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{2 \\cdot 3}{a+b} = \\frac{3}{2} \\implies \\frac{6}{a+b} = \\frac{3}{2} \\implies 6 \\cdot 2 = 3(a+b) \\implies 12 = 3(a+b) \\implies a+b = 4\n\\]\n\nNow we have the equations:\n\\[\nab = 3 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad a+b = 4\n\\]\n\nThese are the same equations we have if we solve $a$ and $b$ as the roots of the quadratic equation $t^2 - (a+b)t + ab = 0$:\n\\[\nt^2 - 4t + 3 = 0\n\\]\n\nWe solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula:\n\\[\nt = \\frac{4 \\pm \\sqrt{16 - 12}}{2} = \\frac{4 \\pm 2}{2}\n\\]\nThis gives us two solutions:\n\\[\nt = \\frac{4 + 2}{2} = 3 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad t = \\frac{4 - 2}{2} = 1\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the two numbers are $1$ and $3$. The final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1, 3}\n\\]",
