      "text": "Let the two positive real numbers be \\( a \\) and \\( b \\). We are given the following information:\n\n1. The geometric mean of \\( a \\) and \\( b \\) is \\( \\sqrt{3} \\).\n2. The harmonic mean of \\( a \\) and \\( b \\) is \\( \\frac{3}{2} \\).\n\nThe geometric mean of \\( a \\) and \\( b \\) is given by:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{ab} = \\sqrt{3}\n\\]\nSquaring both sides, we get:\n\\[\nab = 3\n\\]\n\nThe harmonic mean of \\( a \\) and \\( b \\) is given by:\n\\[\n\\frac{2ab}{a + b} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\nSubstituting \\( ab = 3 \\) into the equation, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{2 \\cdot 3}{a + b} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\nSimplifying, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{6}{a + b} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\nCross-multiplying gives:\n\\[\n12 = 3(a + b)\n\\]\nDividing both sides by 3, we get:\n\\[\na + b = 4\n\\]\n\nNow we have a system of equations:\n\\[\nab = 3\n\\]\n\\[\na + b = 4\n\\]\n\nWe can solve this system by treating \\( a \\) and \\( b \\) as the roots of the quadratic equation:\n\\[\nx^2 - (a + b)x + ab = 0\n\\]\nSubstituting the known values, we get:\n\\[\nx^2 - 4x + 3 = 0\n\\]\n\nWe can solve this quadratic equation using factoring:\n\\[\nx^2 - 4x + 3 = (x - 1)(x - 3) = 0\n\\]\nSo the solutions are:\n\\[\nx = 1 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x = 3\n\\]\nTherefore, the two numbers are \\( 1 \\) and \\( 3 \\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1, 3}\n\\]",
